<section class="source-text source-heading project-section" style="--source-space:95.99981689453125px;--source-height:220px" data-source-section="1477:3012"><div data-node-id="1477:3012" data-name="Brand Story" class="content-stretch flex flex-col gap-[18px] h-[220px] items-start overflow-clip py-[64px] relative shrink-0 w-[1344px]"><div data-node-id="1477:3013" data-name="Divider" class="h-px relative shrink-0 w-[1344px]"><img alt="" src="/assets/parity/1206-1212-6854e.svg" loading="lazy" decoding="async" class="absolute block inset-0 max-w-none size-full"></div><p data-node-id="1477:3014" class="[word-break:break-word] font-['Hanken_Grotesk'] font-bold font-bold leading-[1.6] relative shrink-0 text-[#0a0a0a] text-[length:12px] tracking-[0.96px] uppercase w-[500px]">BRAND STORY</p><p data-node-id="1477:3015" class="[word-break:break-word] font-['Bebas_Neue'] leading-[1.05] not-italic relative shrink-0 text-[#0a0a0a] text-[68px] tracking-[0.68px] uppercase whitespace-nowrap">COMFORT WAS NEVER IN THE FABRIC. IT WAS IN THE CARE.</p></div></section>
<section class="source-text source-copy project-section" style="--source-space:96px;--source-height:320px" data-source-section="1477:3029"><div data-node-id="1477:3029" data-name="Case Block / The Approach" class="content-stretch flex gap-[60px] h-[320px] items-start overflow-clip relative shrink-0 w-[1344px]"><div data-node-id="1477:3030" data-name="Label" class="content-stretch flex flex-col h-[320px] items-start overflow-clip relative shrink-0 w-[330px]"><p data-node-id="1477:3031" class="[word-break:break-word] font-['Hanken_Grotesk'] font-bold font-bold leading-[1.6] relative shrink-0 text-[#0a0a0a] text-[length:12px] tracking-[0.96px] uppercase w-[300px]">THE APPROACH</p></div><div data-node-id="1477:3032" data-name="Copy" class="content-stretch flex flex-col h-[320px] items-start overflow-clip relative shrink-0 w-[954px]"><p data-node-id="1477:3033" class="[word-break:break-word] font-['Hanken_Grotesk'] font-normal leading-[1.5] relative shrink-0 text-[#0a0a0a] text-[length:22px] w-[930px]">We started with the story rather than the surface. The existing brand had credible material truth: eucalyptus Lyocell, softness, thermoregulation and a real following in the DACH market. Rather than replace that foundation, we reframed its role. The product would remain the proof. Care would become the meaning. From there, the work expanded beyond colour and interface into a complete brand world — photography, motion, packaging, editorial language, digital experience and customer touchpoints. The goal was not to create more assets. It was to define a set of behaviours that could make Cozy Heaven feel coherent wherever it appeared.</p></div></div></section>
